## Ratchet rule

New code meets the standard. Touched code is brought to the standard within the
boundary of the change. Untouched code is grandfathered and listed in `DEBT.md`.

This is what keeps declared standards from failing on day one against
pre-existing violations, which is how gates get disabled within a week.

